    {"id":"skill-review","hard":false,"changes":false,"skillCase":true,"moreCase":false,"skills":["code-review"],"asked":[],"passed":true,"problem":null,"calls":[{"tool":"git_status","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"git_diff","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src\\cart.py"}},{"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src\\cart.py"}},{"tool":"run_tests","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"list_directory","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"list_directory","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src"}},{"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src\\cart.py"}}],"seconds":20.24,"tokens":668,"promptTokens":2836,"keptTokens":2385,"readTokens":451,"readSeconds":0.840,"readTokensPerSecond":537,"writtenTokens":668,"writeSeconds":18.790,"writtenTokensPerSecond":35.6,"toolCalls":8,"toolCallWriteMs":5454,"toolRunMs":0,"guessed":613,"guessesTaken":358,"toolTimes":[{"tool":"git_status","writeMs":683,"runMs":0},{"tool":"git_diff","writeMs":673,"runMs":0},{"tool":"read_file","writeMs":707,"runMs":0},{"tool":"read_file","writeMs":718,"runMs":0},{"tool":"run_tests","writeMs":699,"runMs":0},{"tool":"list_directory","writeMs":605,"runMs":0},{"tool":"list_directory","writeMs":648,"runMs":0},{"tool":"read_file","writeMs":721,"runMs":0}],"answer":"I reviewed the uncommitted change in `src/cart.py` (the only modified file).\n\n## Bugs\n\n**1. Discount is applied twice** — `src/cart.py`, `line_total`\n\n```python\ntotal = price * quantity * (1 - discount)\n# members get their discount\ntotal = total * (1 - discount)\n```\n\nThe discount is multiplied in twice, so a 10% discount becomes 19% off (0.9 × 0.9 = 0.81). For a $100 item at 10% off, the customer pays $81 instead of $90. Fix: apply it once.\n\n```python\ntotal = price * quantity * (1 - discount)\nreturn round(total, 2)\n```\n\n**2. `round(total, 2)` is new and may break callers** — the old code returned the raw float. If any caller compares `line_total(...)` to an unrounded value (e.g. `assert line_total(1.99, 3, 0.1) == 5.373`), it will now fail. Rounding to cents is usually the right call for money, but check the callers before committing.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **No validation of `discount`**: a discount > 1 (e.g. `1.5`) makes the total negative; a negative discount inflates it. The old code had the same gap, so this isn't a regression, but worth a `0 <= discount <= 1` guard while you're in here.\n\n## Clean-ups\n\n- The `# members get their discount` comment describes intent that the code no longer matches — remove it with the duplicate line.\n\n## Looks good\n\n- The `quantity <= 0` early return is a clearer guard than the old `if quantity > 0` / `return "},
